It's not too hard to stump me, as I'm far from an expert, but
this dumps core on my RH7.0 Alpha Linux box, too.  My first
thought was that there should probably be an 'l' in front of the
'f' in the format string.  I tried all four combinations of 'l'
vs. no 'l' in front of the 'd' and 'f'.  All four core dump.  A
check with gdb says the problem happens in the printf call, at
line 270 of vfprintf.c, and at line 203 of dl-runtime.c, at their
respective levels on the stack.  I don't find either of these
files on my system, so I would guess they are in the GLIBC
sources.

Good luck.

