> I am working as a customer service engineer, for some years on Intel
> based linux machines and AlphaServers with Digital Unix. I would like
> to try installing linux on an AlphaServer 1000, using only the source
> code.

Good luck !

> Don't tell me please to buy a distribusion for Alpha. I know this is
> tbe best way, and it will save me from a lot of trouble. I just want
> to experiment and learn from it.
> I would appreciate any advice or help on how to get started.

Well have a read of the Linux-From-Scratch-HOWTO and the Alpha-HOWTO
to start with. However even the former doesn't really start from
scratch, it starts from a working Linux system, from which you can
effectively build your own distribution.

To do it totally from scratch would need a /lot/ of boot-strapping.
How do you compile your compiler, your editor, kernel, shell, blah 
starting from nothing ? Though you could go one level back from
building it on a Linux system, if you wanted you could build
on any platform that you can find with a working gcc cross-compiler.
So also see the GCC-HOWTO and I'm sure there's one about
setting it up for cross-compilation.

