The 164UX has somewhat special requirements--which
michal@gortel.phys.ualberta.ca summarized in another message--and
I'm not sure those are supported by the installation routines
offered by current distributions.  Which doesn't mean that an
installation is impossible, it may just mean that you need to do
stuff manually and need to know what you are doing rather than just
clicking "Yes".

> I don�t know the differences between the 164UX and 164LX,
       ^
(That's an acute accent, not an apostrophe.)

As far as the firmware is concerned, the 164LX offers a choice of
SRM or AlphaBIOS.  The 164UX is limited to ARCSBIOS, which is not
the same as AlphaBIOS.

