I presume you meant an AXPpci33, a.k.a. NoName board.  Yes, it's perfectly 
BAT-standard. Even the ribbon cables are pc-standard. All you need is a fan,
since those beasts get hot as hell. You can even cook your beans on the CPU
w/o cooling.  Regarding them video cards, I have a Permedia2-based card in
my box. Matrox should do fine as well. Controller cards shouldn't bring up 
any problems, as long as they are supported by Linux. Finding native parts 
for this baby seems to be quite hard. You might try www.islandco.com. I 
went for some cache without success (Does any1 have 1MB to give away for a 
decent price?).  But don't expect too much of it.  If my information is 
correct, a 21066 @ 166MHz compares to a 75MHz Pentium I.  Correct me if I'm 
wrong, but that seems to be fairly accurate.  Nevertheless, an Alpha is a 
totally different kind of animal compared to a PC. It is worth the try.


Marc



