The solution to this is probably simply to use a big enough fan to blow 
air trough the cooling rips of the CPU. The OEM design guide that 
should come with the board (I was lucky to get one) clearily specifies 
that though the board is only equipped with a passive cooler, you need 
to find and place a fan before the cooler to blow air parally through 
the rips.

